.TH TUIDESK 1 2026-10-31 "tuidesk 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tuidesk \- a KDE Plasma style desktop for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuidesk
.RB [ \-S
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\-standalone ]
.br
.B tuidesk ls
.br
.B tuidesk kill
.RB [ \-S
.IR name ]
.br
.B tuidesk msg
.IR command " [" argument ...]
.br
.B tuidesk
.BR \-\-print\-config " | " \-\-print\-lua " | " \-\-print\-apps
.br
.B tuidesk
.BR \-h " | " \-V
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tuidesk
runs a desktop inside a terminal: floating and tiled windows with title bars, virtual
desktops, a panel with a launcher, pager, task manager and clock, a KRunner style runner,
an overview of all windows, notifications and screenshots.
Every window is a real pseudo\-terminal, so any program runs in it, including full screen
programs such as
.BR nvim (1),
.BR htop (1)
or
.BR yazi (1).
.PP
Like
.BR tmux (1),
.B tuidesk
runs a background server per session that owns the windows and their programs; the terminal
it is started in is a client.
Detaching (prefix key, then
.BR d )
or closing the terminal leaves the desktop running, and running
.B tuidesk
again reattaches to it.
Attaching from another terminal detaches the one that was attached.
.PP
Sessions are saved on quit, on detach and every 30 seconds, and the windows, their working
directories, geometry and desktops are restored when a server starts.
.PP
On Windows there is no background server:
.B tuidesk
runs in the terminal it is started in, as with
.BR \-\-standalone ,
and
.BR ls ,
.BR kill ,
.B msg
and detaching are not available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-session " \fIname\fR"
Use the session
.IR name ,
starting its server if needed.
The default is
.BR default ,
or the session of the window
.B tuidesk
runs in
.RB ( $TUIDESK_SESSION ).
Names are up to 32 letters, digits,
.BR \- ,
.B _
or
.BR . ,
and do not start with a dot.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIdir\fR"
Read
.B config.toml
and
.B init.lua
from
.I dir
instead of the default configuration directory.
.TP
.B \-\-standalone
Run the desktop in this terminal only, without a background server.
Detaching is not possible, and the desktop ends with the terminal.
Refuses to start while a background server owns the same session name.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Print the built\-in
.B config.toml
and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-lua
Print the built\-in
.B init.lua
and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-apps
Print the built\-in catalogue of launcher entries and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR ls ", " list
List the running sessions.
.TP
.BR kill ", " kill\-server
Save the session and stop its server, closing all its windows.
.TP
.BI msg " command"
Send a command to a running session and print its answer.
Inside a
.B tuidesk
window this talks to that window's session.
.RS
.TP
.BI notify " title \fR[\fPbody\fR...]"
Show a notification.
.TP
.BI spawn " command\fR..."
Open a window running
.IR command ;
prints the new window's id.
.TP
.B windows
List the windows: id, desktop, focus (marked
.BR * ),
title and command.
.TP
.BI focus " id" "\fR, \fPclose" " id"
Focus or close a window.
.TP
.B desktops
Print the current desktop and the number of desktops.
.TP
.BR screenshot " [" screen | window | \fIid\fR "] [" txt | ansi | html | svg "] [\fIpath\fR]"
Save a screenshot and print its path.
Relative paths are taken from the directory
.B tuidesk msg
runs in.
.TP
.BI lua " code"
Run Lua in the plugin environment and print the results.
.TP
.IR action " [" argument ]
Run any key binding action (see
.BR tuidesk\-config (5)),
for example
.BR "desktop 2" ,
.B "layout grid"
or
.BR detach .
.TP
.B help
List these commands.
.RE
.SH KEYS
Terminals cannot report the Super key, so window management uses a
.I prefix key
.RB ( ctrl+space
by default) followed by another key, plus a few direct shortcuts.
Pressing the prefix key twice sends it to the program.
All bindings can be changed in
.B [keys.prefix]
and
.B [keys.global]
of the configuration file, or in System Settings.
.SS After the prefix key
.TP 14
.BR space
Kickoff launcher.
.TP
.BR enter ", " c
New terminal window.
.TP
.B x
Close the window.
.TP
.BR m ", " up
Maximize or restore.
.TP
.B n
Minimize.
.TP
.BR tab ", " shift+tab
Next or previous window.
.TP
.BR 1 .. 9 ", " . ", " ,
Go to desktop
.IR n ,
the next or the previous desktop.
.TP
.BR > ", " <
Move the window to the next or previous desktop and follow it.
.TP
.BR h ", " l ", " k ", " j
Quick tile left, right, top or bottom (in a tiled layout: move the window).
The arrow keys do the same.
.TP
.BR t ", " T
Toggle floating and tiled layout; cycle through all layouts.
.TP
.B f
Float or unfloat the window in a tiled layout.
.TP
.B s
Swap the window with the master.
.TP
.B w
Keyboard move and resize mode.
.TP
.B [
Copy mode (see
.BR "COPY MODE" ).
.TP
.BR ] ", " p
Paste the last copy.
.TP
.B v
Clipboard history.
.TP
.B ?
Key binding cheat sheet; type to filter.
.TP
.B o
Window menu.
.TP
.B a
Keep the window above others.
.TP
.B R
Rename the window.
.TP
.B W
Overview of all windows on all desktops.
.TP
.BR P ", " ctrl+p ", " alt+p
Screenshot of the screen, the focused window, or a dragged region.
.TP
.B b
Notification history.
.TP
.B S
System Settings.
.TP
.BR e ", " y
Launch the Editor or Files entry.
.TP
.B r
Runner (see
.BR RUNNER ).
.TP
.B ctrl+r
Reload the configuration.
.TP
.B d
Detach.
.TP
.B q
Quit: save the session and close all windows.
.SS Direct shortcuts
.TP 14
.BR alt+f1
Kickoff launcher.
.TP
.B alt+f2
Runner.
.TP
.B alt+tab
Window switcher: hold Alt and press Tab to step, release Alt to pick.
On terminals without the kitty keyboard protocol the highlighted window is picked after a
short pause or on Enter.
.TP
.B alt+enter
New terminal window.
.TP
.BR alt+f4 ", " alt+f9 ", " alt+f10
Close, minimize, maximize.
.TP
.B ctrl+f9
Overview.
.TP
.BR ctrl+f1 .. ctrl+f4
Go to desktop 1 to 4.
.TP
.BR shift+pageup ", " shift+pagedown
Scroll the window's history.
.PP
On macOS, Alt shortcuts need the terminal to send Option as Meta (Terminal.app: \(lqUse
Option as Meta key\(rq; iTerm2: Left Option key sends Esc+).
The prefix key works without this.
.SH MOUSE
Drag a title bar to move a window and its edges to resize it; Alt+drag moves and
Alt+right\-drag resizes from anywhere in the window.
Double\-click a title bar to maximize, middle\-click it to send the window to the back,
right\-click it for the window menu.
Dragging a window to a screen edge tiles it to that side.
.PP
In the panel, click a task to focus or minimize it, middle\-click it to close it, and drag
it onto a desktop in the pager to move it there.
Scroll over the panel to cycle windows, or over the pager to change desktops.
Right\-click a desktop in the pager to rename it.
.PP
Dragging inside a window selects text (double\-click selects a word, triple\-click a line);
the selection is copied to the clipboard history and to the host terminal's clipboard with
OSC 52.
Middle\-click pastes.
Hold Shift to select in programs that use the mouse themselves.
Ctrl+click opens an OSC 8 hyperlink.
.SH RUNNER
The runner searches as you type and mixes results from several sources:
an arithmetic expression such as
.B 2*(3+4)
or
.B sqrt(2)
is calculated (Enter copies the result);
a window title switches to that window;
an application name launches it;
a path such as
.B ~/src/pro
lists directories (Enter opens a shell there, Tab completes);
.BI man " page"
opens a manual page;
action names such as
.B layout grid
run that action;
anything else can be run as a command.
.SH COPY MODE
Copy mode moves a cursor through the window and its history.
.TP 18
.BR h " " j " " k " " l ", " w " " b " " e
Move by character, line and word.
.TP
.BR 0 " " ^ " " $ ", " H " " M " " L ", " g " " G
Line start and end, screen top, middle and bottom, history start and end.
.TP
.BR ctrl+u " " ctrl+d " " ctrl+b " " ctrl+f
Half and full pages.
.TP
.BR / ", " ? ", " n ", " N
Search forward or backward with a regular expression (case\-insensitive unless it contains
capitals), repeat.
.TP
.BR v ", " V ", " ctrl+v
Select characters, lines or a block.
.TP
.BR y ", " enter
Copy and leave.
.TP
.B q
Leave.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TUIDESK_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory for the session sockets and server logs.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Used for sockets as
.B $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/tuidesk
when
.B TUIDESK_RUNTIME_DIR
is not set; otherwise
.BI /tmp/tuidesk\- uid
is used.
The directory must belong to the user and is kept at mode 0700.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Configuration directory base (default
.BR ~/.config ).
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Saved session directory base (default
.BR ~/.local/state ).
.TP
.B SHELL
Shell for new terminal windows when
.B general.shell
is empty; otherwise
.BR /bin/sh .
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor for notes widgets.
.TP
.BR TUIDESK ", " TUIDESK_SESSION
Set inside every window.
.B TUIDESK
stops a nested desktop from starting;
.B TUIDESK_SESSION
makes
.B tuidesk msg
talk to the window's own session.
.TP
.BR TERM ", " COLORTERM ", " TERM_PROGRAM
Used to choose the color depth and the image protocol of the host terminal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tuidesk/config.toml
Configuration, created on first start and reloaded when saved; see
.BR tuidesk\-config (5).
.TP
.I ~/.config/tuidesk/init.lua
Lua plugins, created on first start and reloaded when saved; see
.BR tuidesk\-lua (7).
.TP
.I ~/.config/tuidesk/lua/
Lua modules that
.B init.lua
can
.BR require .
.TP
.IR ~/.local/state/tuidesk/session\- name .json
Saved session.
A file that cannot be read is kept as
.IB name .json.bak
instead of being overwritten.
.TP
.IR ~/Pictures/tuidesk/
Screenshots (setting
.BR screenshot.dir ).
.TP
.IR $TUIDESK_RUNTIME_DIR/ name ".sock, " name .log
A session's socket and server log.
.PP
On Windows the configuration is in
.I %APPDATA%\(rstuidesk
and saved sessions are in
.IR %LOCALAPPDATA%\(rstuidesk .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B tuidesk
exits 0 on success and 1 on an error, such as a session that cannot be reached, a socket
directory owned by another user, or a
.B tuidesk msg
command that failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start a separate desktop for work, detach from it, and come back later:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tuidesk \-S work
# prefix key, then d
tuidesk \-S work
.fi
.RE
.PP
Open a window and notify when a build finishes, from a script or cron job:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tuidesk msg spawn btop
make && tuidesk msg notify Build "make finished"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Save a screenshot of the focused window as SVG:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tuidesk msg screenshot window svg shot.svg
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tuidesk\-config (5),
.BR tuidesk\-lua (7),
.BR tmux (1),
.BR screen (1)
